				"1578A7A80B07816E"
			]
			description: [
				"The &2generator&r consumes SU to generate electricity. The faster it spins, the more voltage and power it creates, up to a maximum of &3255V&r and &c12.1kW&r. More nerd details on the next page."
				""
				"This is a multi-step deploying recipe, with one step involving the &ewinding machine&r."
				"Start with a &6shaft&r and do the following steps:"
				""
				"1. Capacitor"
				"2. Heavy plate"
				"3. Use a &ewinding machine&r to wrap 75 turns of &6copper wire&r around it."
				"4. Magnet"
				"5. Steel mechanism"
				"6. Screwdriver"
				""
				"Repeat this three times for an 83% chance of getting a generator."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&30RPM - 40RPM&r"
				"No electricity generation"
				""
				"&341RPM - 223RPM&r"
				"Linear voltage rise from 1V - 255V"
				"Constant current limit of 40A, thus power output ranges from 40W - 10.2kW"
				""
				"&3224RPM - 256RPM&r"
				"Constant 255V with increasing power output up to 12.1kW"
				"Current limit increases to 47.5A"
			]
			icon: "tfmg:generator"
			id: "52D8B15C3B75AB7F"
