			dependencies: ["138B96B20044ED12"]
			description: [
				"Potentiometers let a &bpercentage&r of the input voltage to the output side. Unlike real life, they do not waste power."
				""
				"For example, if your base is wired at &33kV&r, but you only need &3150V&r for your lights, you can set up a potentiometer for the lights at 5%. This way, they don't eat several kW of power for zero gain."
				""
				"The vaguely arrow shaped end of the block is the output."
